                        <h5 style="color:orange">Course Highlights:</h5>
                        <br />
                        <p>
                            In 2025 and 2026, data analytics courses are evolving to bridge the gap between traditional data management and AI-integrated workflows. The key highlights of these programs typically include a combination of technical mastery, hands-on project work, and specialized AI training.
                        </p>
                        <ul>

                            <li>

                                <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>
                                    Core Technical Curriculum
                                </b> :
                                <p style="margin-left:2%">
                                    Modern courses focus on a "foundational four" toolset essential for professional readiness
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>
                                            <b>Excel (Basic & Advanced):</b>
                                            <p style="margin-left:2%">
                                                Vectors, matrices, eigenvalues, and Singular Value Decomposition (SVD).
                                            </p>
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            <b>SQL (Mandatory):</b>
                                            <p style="margin-left:2%">
                                                Mastering database querying, complex joins, subqueries, and window functions.
                                            </p>
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            <b>Python/R:</b>
                                            <p style="margin-left:2%">
                                                Learning programming specifically for data manipulation (using libraries like Pandas and NumPy) and statistical modeling.
                                            </p>
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            <b>Visualization Tools:</b>
                                            <p style="margin-left:2%">
                                                Hands-on training in <b>Tableau</b> or <b>Power BI</b> to build interactive business dashboards and practice data storytelling.
                                            </p>
                                        </li>
                                    </ul>
                                </p>

                            </li>
                            <li>

                                <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i> <b>
                                    AI and Emerging Tech Integration

                                </b> :
